2.LUCAS NUMBER 
A Lucas Number is a number which is represented by the following recurrence
Ln = Ln-1 + Ln-2 for n>1
L0 = 2
L1 = 1
Given a number n, find the nth lucas number.
Note: Since the output may be very large calculate the answer modulus 10^9+7.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public long lucas(int n) {
                long max=1000000007;
                if(n<2){
                    return n==0?2:1;
                }
                long a=2,b=1;
                for(int i=2;i<=n;i++){
                    long c=(a+b)%max;
                    a=b;
                    b=c;
                }
                return b;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/lucas-number4515/1


3.MINIMUM NUMBER OF COINS 
Given an infinite supply of each denomination of Indian currency { 1, 2, 5, 10 } and a target value n. 
Find the minimum number of coins and/or notes needed to make the change for Rs n. 
SOURCE CODE 
class Solution {
    public int findMin(int n) {
        int count=0;
        count+=n/10;
        n%=10;
        count+=n/5;
        n%=5;
        count+=n/2;
        n%=2;
        count+=n;
        return count;
    }
}
