4.MINIMUM OPERATIONS 
Given a number n. Find the minimum number of operations required to reach n starting from 0. You have two operations available:
Double the number
Add one to the number
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int minOperation(int n) {
                int count=0;
                while(n>0){
                     if((n&1)==0){
                         n/=2;
                     }
                     else{
                         n--;
                     }
                     count++;
                }
                return count;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/find-optimum-operation4504/1


5.FIRST N FIBONACCI USING RECURSION 
Given a number n, return an array containing the first n Fibonacci numbers.
Note: The first two numbers of the series are 0 and 1.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public static int[] fibonacciNumbers(int n) {
                int arr[]=new int[n];
                for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
                    arr[i]=fib(i);
                }
                return arr;
            }
            public static int fib(int num){
                if(num<=1){
                    return num;
                }
                else{
                    return fib(num-2)+fib(num-1);
                }
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/print-first-n-fibonacci-numbers1002/1


6.POWER OF FOUR 
Given a number n, check if n is power of 4 or not.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            boolean isPowerOfFour(int n) {
                if(n<=0){
                    return false;
                }
                if(n==1){
                    return true;
                }
                while(n>1){
                    if(n%4!=0){
                        return false;
                    }
                    n/=4;
                }
                return true;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/power-of-four/1


7.CHECK POWER OF 3
Given a positive integer n, find if it is a power of 3. A number is said to be a power of 3 if it can be expressed as 3x for some non-negative integer x.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            static boolean isPowerOf3(int n) {
                if(n<=0){
                    return false;
                }
                while(n%3==0){
                    n/=3;
                }
                return n==1;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/check-a-integer-is-power-of-3-or-not3850/1


8.CHECK FOR POWER 
Given two positive integers x and y, determine if y is a power of x. If y is a power of x, return true. Otherwise, return false.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public boolean isPower(int x, int y) {
                if(x<=0 || y<=0 || x==1){
                    return false;
                }
                while(y%x==0){
                    if(y%x!=0){
                        return false;
                    }
                    y/=x;
                }
                return y==1;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/check-if-a-number-is-power-of-another-number5442/1
